      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The difference in the two progressions is $10 - 2 = 8$, so we are looking for a number that is twice a common multiple of 7 and 8, i. e., of $84$.\nIf we compare the two first terms with 500, we have $196$ and $280$ respectively, so the largest common value less than 500 is of the form $$280 + 84k, \\text{ where } k\\in \\mathbb{N} \\text{ and } 196 < 280 + 84k < 500.$$\nIf we put $280 + 84k = 196$ or $280 + 84k = 500$, we obtain $k = 2$ or $k = 2.843, \\text{ with } 2.843 \\not\\in \\mathbb{N}$. So the last step is $280 + 84\\cdot2 = \\boxed{468.}$",
